                      LWF For OS9/68000Ported 4/11/1995 Russell Hoffman, reh@fore.comLWF is an ASCII-to-PostScript convertor utility that runs underOS9/68000. It serves a purpose similar to that of the Unix "enscript"command; it allows you to print plain ASCII to a PostScript printer. I ported this utility because up until now, when I wanted to print anASCII file on my printer from my OSK box, I had to load the documentinto TeX (many thanks to Tim Kientzle!), format it, run TeX, and thendvi_alw. Needless to say, this was too much work!I did a quick and dirty port, which works for my purposes, but I havenot tested all the features of the original LWF program. Inparticular, the following are untested:   o Page reversal option   o Piping the ASCII text thru the optional "pr" filter.Compiling the source requires the TOP os9lib.l library. Look in theMakefile for details. One deficiency is the hostname lookup function. LWF prints the userand hostname on the optional banner page. I could have easily addedthe TOP hostname call to get the hostname from the string stored insysinfo, but I imagined that would be less broadly useable, especiallyfor users not running TOP sysinfo. Simply recompile with HOSTNAMEdefined to whatever value you like in the Makefile. Any deficiencies found with this port I will gladly resolve. I'mposting this early first-run port now mainly because I think itsusefulness outweighs its state of unfinishedness. Both ported and original code are included in this distribution, withmy thanks to the original author!Russell Hoffmanreh@fore.comFORE Systems, Inc. 